00:11:55,790 --> 00:11:58,080
Ugly Naked Guy lit a bunch of candles.

281
00:12:05,090 --> 00:12:06,910
That had to hurt!

282
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:12,030
Hey, it's your Thanksgiving too.

283
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,620
Instead of watching football,

284
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:14,760
you could help.

285
00:12:14,810 --> 00:12:15,950
We know.

286
00:12:17,470 --> 00:12:19,680
Rachel, you want to put the marshmallows

287
00:12:19,730 --> 00:12:20,880
in concentric circles.

288
00:12:20,930 --> 00:12:21,850
No, Mon.

289
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:24,100
You want to put them in concentric circles.

290
00:12:24,150 --> 00:12:26,080
I want to do this.

291
00:12:35,570 --> 00:12:36,740
Every year.

292
00:12:40,570 --> 00:12:41,990
It's stuck!

293
00:12:43,450 --> 00:12:44,950
Step.

294
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,460
How did it get on?

295
00:12:46,510 --> 00:12:49,260
I put it on to scare Chandler.

296
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:51,130
Oh, my God!

297
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:53,430
Monica's going to totally freak out!

298
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,670
Plus, it smells really bad in here.

299
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,310
Of course it smells bad.

300
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:00,070
You have your head up a turkey's ass.

301
00:13:02,930 --> 00:13:03,930
Monica.

302
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:08,000
Did you get the turkey--?

303
00:13:08,050 --> 00:13:10,100
Oh, my God!

304
00:13:11,310 --> 00:13:12,510
Who is that?

305
00:13:12,790 --> 00:13:14,100
It's Joey.

306
00:13:15,310 --> 00:13:16,250
I got it!

307
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:17,930
If we win,

308
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:19,610
they have to get rid of the rooster.

309
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:21,340
That's interesting!

310
00:13:22,850 --> 00:13:24,220
If you win...

311
00:13:24,550 --> 00:13:26,000
...we give up the bird.

312
00:13:29,230 --> 00:13:30,310
But if we win...

313
00:13:31,410 --> 00:13:32,870
...we get your apartment.

314
00:13:36,510 --> 00:13:37,870
- Deal! - What?

315
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:40,330
"What was Monica's nickname

316
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:42,050
when she was a hockey goalie?"

317
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:43,550
- Big Fat Goalie. - Correct!

318
00:13:45,270 --> 00:13:47,760
"Rachel claims it's her favorite movie."

319
00:13:47,810 --> 00:13:49,110
Dangerous Liaisons.

320
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:50,830
Correct, "Her actual favorite movie is...?"

321
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:51,940
Weekend at Bernie's.

322
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:56,100
"Monica categorizes her towels.

323
00:13:56,150 --> 00:13:58,270
How many categories are there?"

324
00:13:58,320 --> 00:13:59,750
- Everyday use. - Fancy.

325
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,400
- Guest. - Fancy guest.

326
00:14:01,450 --> 00:14:03,530
- Two seconds. - Eleven?

327
00:14:04,530 --> 00:14:06,860
Eleven! Unbelievable! Eleven is correct.

328
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:10,080
"Chandler was how old

329
00:14:10,130 --> 00:14:11,740
when he first touched a girl's breast?"

330
00:14:11,790 --> 00:14:13,200
- 14? - No, 19.

331
00:14:13,250 --> 00:14:14,270
Thanks, man.

332
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:17,780
"Joey had an imaginary childhood friend.

333
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:19,140
- His name was...?" - Maurice!

334
00:14:19,140 --> 00:14:20,590
Correct! "His profession was...?"

335
00:14:20,590 --> 00:14:22,000
Space cowboy!

336
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:25,420
"What is Chandler Bing's job?"

337
00:14:31,050 --> 00:14:31,710
Ten seconds.

338
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:32,900
You need this or you lose.

339
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:35,770
Something to do with transponding.

340
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:38,560
He's a transpons...transponster!

341
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,570
That's not even a word!

342
00:14:52,010 --> 00:14:54,690
You are mean boys

343
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:55,940
who are just being mean!

344
00:14:55,990 --> 00:14:57,560
Don't get mad!

345
00:14:57,610 --> 00:14:59,450
No one forced you to raise the stakes.

346
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:02,240
That is not true! She forced me!

347
00:15:02,290 --> 00:15:03,480
Hey, we would still be living here

348
00:15:03,530 --> 00:15:04,840
if you hadn't gotten the question wrong!

349
00:15:04,890 --> 00:15:07,420
It was a stupid, unfair question!

350
00:15:07,470 --> 00:15:09,180
Don't blame the questions!

351
00:15:09,310 --> 00:15:11,680
Stop yelling in our apartment!

352
00:15:11,730 --> 00:15:14,040
You are ruining moving day for us.

353
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:16,450
Chandler!

354
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:22,520
I saw what you were doing in the window!

355
00:15:22,570 --> 00:15:24,600
I saw what you're doing to my sister!

356
00:15:24,650 --> 00:15:25,930
Get out here!

357
00:15:27,150 --> 00:15:28,920
Listen, we had a good run.

358
00:15:29,530 --> 00:15:31,660
What was it? Four, five months?

359
00:15:31,710 --> 00:15:32,710
I mean that's more

360
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:33,950
than most people have in a lifetime.

361
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,360
So, goodbye, take care, byebye.

362
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:38,350
Hey, Ross.

363
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:39,230
What's up, bro?

364
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:45,730
What the hell are you doing?

365
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:46,830
What's going on?

366
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:50,630
I think...I think Ross knows about me and Monica.

367
00:15:52,190 --> 00:15:54,260
Dude, he's right there.

368
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:58,250
I thought you were my best friend!

369
00:15:58,300 --> 00:15:59,850
This is my sister!

370
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:01,560
My best friend and my sister!

371
00:16:01,610 --> 00:16:03,210
I cannot believe this!

372
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:05,370
We're not just messing around.

373
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:06,720
I love her.

374
00:16:07,430 --> 00:16:08,880
I'm in love with her.

375
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:11,120
I'm so sorry

376
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:12,670
that you had to find out this way.

377
00:16:14,050 --> 00:16:15,570
I'm sorry, but it's true.

378
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:16,860
I love him too.

379
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:26,510
My best friend and my sister!

380
00:16:29,170 --> 00:16:31,540
I cannot believe this!

381
00:16:32,530 --> 00:16:34,770
This is the last box of your clothes.

382
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:36,150
I'm just gonna label it

383
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,600
"What were you thinking?"

384
00:16:39,150 --> 00:16:41,580
I was gonna go across the hall

385
00:16:41,630 --> 00:16:43,190
and write that on Chandler.

386
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,550
Guys, I don't mean to make things worse, but...

387
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,850
...l don't want to live with Rachel anymore.

388
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:51,720
-What? -What?

389
00:16:51,770 --> 00:16:53,820
You're so mean to each other.

390
00:16:53,870 --> 00:16:55,940
I don't wanna end up like that with Rachel.

391
00:16:55,990 --> 00:16:57,240
I still like you.

392
00:16:57,760 --> 00:17:00,240
That's fine because I'm not moving.

393
00:17:01,410 --> 00:17:02,910
Phoebe, you gotta take her.

394
00:17:04,220 --> 00:17:06,050
You know, I know I said some bad stuff...

395
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:08,370
...but Rachel has qualities

396
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:09,530
that make her a good roommate.

397
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:11,710
She gets tons of catalogs and she folds

398
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:14,420
she folds down the pages of things she thinks I'd like.

399
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:15,950
What else?

400
00:17:17,850 --> 00:17:19,230
When I take a shower...

401
00:17:20,030 --> 00:17:21,900
...she leaves me notes on the mirror.

402
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:24,000
I do. I do do that.

403
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,060
That's nice.

404
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,400
I like having things to read in the bathroom.

405
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:33,590
When I fall asleep on the couch...

406
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:36,460
...she covers me with a blanket.

407
00:17:37,070 --> 00:17:40,580
Well, you know, I don't want you to be cold.

408
00:17:44,190 --> 00:17:44,920
And when I told her

409
00:17:44,970 --> 00:17:46,670
that I was gonna move in with Chandler...

410
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:49,970
...she was really supportive.

411
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,330
You were so great.

412
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:58,220
You made it so easy.

413
00:17:59,940 --> 00:18:02,630
And now you have to leave.

414
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:05,210
And I have to live with a boy!

415
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:24,190
- She really left. - I know.

416
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:29,980
- Thank you. - No problem, roomie.

417
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:40,670
- Can I ask you a question? - Sure.

418
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:43,080
What the hell is that dog doing here?

419
00:18:44,820 --> 00:18:46,770
A little toast here. Ding, ding!

420
00:18:47,670 --> 00:18:48,710
I know this isn't exactly

421
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:50,620
the kind of Thanksgiving you planned...

422
00:18:50,670 --> 00:18:54,180
...but for me this has been really great.

423
00:18:54,230 --> 00:18:56,240
You know, I think because

424
00:18:56,290 --> 00:18:58,270
it didn't involve divorce...

425
00:18:58,320 --> 00:18:59,700
...or projectile vomiting.

426
00:19:02,270 --> 00:19:03,340
Anyway, I think if

427
00:19:03,390 --> 00:19:04,280
you had gone to Vail...

428
00:19:04,330 --> 00:19:06,420
...or if you had been with your family,

429
00:19:06,470 --> 00:19:07,850
or if you didn't have...

430
00:19:08,840 --> 00:19:10,400
...syphilis and stuff...

431
00:19:12,450 --> 00:19:14,740
...we wouldn't be all together.

432
00:19:14,790 --> 00:19:17,020
So I guess what I'm trying to say is...

433
00:19:17,070 --> 00:19:19,190
...that I'm very thankful

434
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:21,990
that all of your Thanksgivings sucked.

435
00:19:23,430 --> 00:19:26,450
- That's so sweet! - Thank you.

436
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,180
Here's to a lousy Christmas!

437
00:19:31,230 --> 00:19:32,790
And a crappy New Year!

438
00:19:32,840 --> 00:19:34,840
Hear, hear!

439
00:19:41,110 --> 00:19:42,150
You can't move.

440
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,380
You just-- You just can't.

441
00:19:43,430 --> 00:19:44,220
Rachel's right.

442
00:19:44,270 --> 00:19:46,090
This is where you guys belong.

443
00:19:46,140 --> 00:19:47,950
Yeah.You don't wanna live in Westchester.

444
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,750
That's the worst of the Chesters.

445
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:51,870
You know,

446
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:53,700
sometimes when I'm alone in my apartment,

447
00:19:53,750 --> 00:19:54,680
I look over here...

448
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:58,090
...and you guys are just having dinner...

449
00:19:58,570 --> 00:20:00,900
...or watching TV or something...

450
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,710
...but it makes me feel better.

451
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:04,890
And now when I look over,

452
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:06,340
who am I gonna see?

453
00:20:06,390 --> 00:20:08,740
The Gottliebs? The Yangs?

454
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:11,960
They don't make me feel so good.

455
00:20:13,270 --> 00:20:15,810
Yeah. So don't move, okay?

456
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:17,310
Just stay here...

457
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:19,360
...and maybe close your blinds at night.

458
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:19,940
Hey.

459
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:27,330
Hello?

460
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:33,090
It's Nancy. They responded to our offer.

461
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:34,130
And?

462
00:20:37,130 --> 00:20:38,620
Okay. Thanks.

463
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:42,410
They passed.

464
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:46,960
They said they won't go a penny under the asking price.

465
00:20:47,270 --> 00:20:49,430
- We can't afford that. - I know.

466
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:53,600
Well, there you go.

467
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:00,060
I'm really sorry, you guys.

468
00:21:00,110 --> 00:21:02,130
Yeah, I'm sorry too.

469
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:04,780
I'm even more sorry that phone call didn't come...

470
00:21:04,830 --> 00:21:06,720
...before I told you about looking through the window.

471
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:10,330
Yeah. Well, we're gonna let you be alone.

472
00:21:10,380 --> 00:21:11,340
You gonna be okay?

473
00:21:11,390 --> 00:21:12,410
Yeah, we'll be okay.

474
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:13,600
Love you guys.

475
00:21:16,260 --> 00:21:17,950
You know, I'm really sorry

476
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,600
I wasn't more supportive before.

477
00:21:19,650 --> 00:21:20,230
That's okay.

478
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:21,070
We understand.

479
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:23,040
Yeah, and about this Nancy....

480
00:21:23,090 --> 00:21:24,930
If you're not sleeping with her, should l?

481
00:21:32,150 --> 00:21:34,740
I know there'll be other houses, but I just--

482
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:37,230
- I love that one so much. - Yeah.

483
00:21:38,650 --> 00:21:40,520
Well, it's a good thing we got it then.

484
00:21:42,300 --> 00:21:44,530
- What? - We got the house.

485
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:46,380
Oh, my God.

486
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:48,150
I didn't wanna tell you in front of them.

487
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:49,940
Oh my god, we got it?! We got the house?!

488
00:21:49,990 --> 00:21:51,350
We're getting a house!

489
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:58,630
- We're getting a house. - And a baby.

490
00:21:58,680 --> 00:21:59,980
We're growing up.

491
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:03,040
We sure are.

492
00:22:04,370 --> 00:22:05,370
- Who's gonna tell them? - Not it!

493
00:22:05,370 --> 00:22:07,000
Not it! Damn it!

494
00:22:12,210 --> 00:22:13,520
Rachel, this is yours.

495
00:22:14,110 --> 00:22:15,980
Why? What are these for?

496
00:22:16,030 --> 00:22:16,960
You'll see.

497
00:22:17,010 --> 00:22:18,810
All right, everybody open them.

498
00:22:21,320 --> 00:22:23,640
Wow, this is so beautiful!

499
00:22:23,690 --> 00:22:26,630
These are the ones I was looking at in the store!

500
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:28,710
- I know. - Oh, I love this!

501
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:30,460
A meatball sub!

502
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:32,590
Thanks!

503
00:22:32,640 --> 00:22:34,420
Seriously, guys, what's going on?

504
00:22:34,470 --> 00:22:35,540
What are these for?

505
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:38,270
Well, I didn't know how to tell you before...

506
00:22:39,080 --> 00:22:40,990
- ...but we got the house. - Enjoy!

507
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:47,430
What did they say?

